# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# PROJECT: the CSP below is the one this system ships with. Adding a third-party
# script, font, or embed means widening it HERE, deliberately, and saying why —
# not discovering at launch that the console is full of blocked requests.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  # 'unsafe-inline' for script-src, and why it is not a nonce: Astro inlines
  # small modules into the HTML, and Pages serves static files — it cannot vary a
  # nonce per response, so a nonce here would be a constant, which is not a
  # nonce. The mitigation is the JS census (§6): every inline module in dist is
  # named and budgeted by `npm run verify`, so "inline script" is an enumerated
  # set rather than an open door.
  # submit-form.com is Formspark, the contact form's endpoint (AUDIT D7). It is
  # named in TWO directives and both are load-bearing:
  #
  #   connect-src — the form is submitted by fetch (src/scripts/contact.ts), and
  #     without this the browser blocks the request outright. That is what
  #     happened when the form moved to Formspark and this file was not followed
  #     through: every submission failed with "Could not reach the server".
  #
  #   form-action — the NO-JAVASCRIPT path. The <form> carries a real action, so
  #     if the module fails to load the browser does a native POST. Under
  #     `form-action 'self'` that POST is blocked and NOTHING VISIBLE HAPPENS —
  #     no navigation, no error on the page, the enquiry simply gone. That is the
  #     silent swallow §8 exists to prevent, so the fallback is allowed to reach
  #     Formspark and land on its thank-you page rather than die quietly.
  #
  # challenges.cloudflare.com is Turnstile, on the contact page only, and it
  # needs THREE directives because it does three things — miss any one and the
  # widget fails differently:
  #
  #   script-src  — the loader, <script src=…/turnstile/v0/api.js>.
  #   frame-src   — Turnstile renders its challenge in an IFRAME. Without this
  #                 the script loads, the widget mounts, and the challenge never
  #                 appears: no token, and every submission refused by Formspark
  #                 for a reason the page cannot explain.
  #   connect-src — the widget calls home to issue and refresh the token.
  #
  # It was removed in AUDIT D7 and is back because the token is verified again —
  # Formspark holds the secret key now. The entry was correctly deleted when
  # nothing checked the token; it is correctly here now that something does.
  #
  # frame-src is declared again for the same reason. It was dropped to inherit
  # default-src 'self', which was tighter and right while nothing framed
  # anything; naming Turnstile is narrower than leaving the directive off would
  # now be.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; media-src 'self' https:; connect-src 'self' https://submit-form.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self' https://submit-form.com; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Fingerprinted assets are immutable: the filename changes when the content does.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML revalidates, so a deploy is visible immediately.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
